	(text_box "FLASHING THE STM32WL55\n---\n\n## 1. Flashing via SWD/JTAG (ST-LINK, Segger J-Link, PyOCD) - *Standard Method*\n\nIf you are using a standard debugger like an **ST-LINK V2/V3** or **J-Link** connected to the SWD pins (`SWCLK` on `PA14` and `SWDIO` on `PA13`):\n\n* **The `BOOT0` button is never needed.**\n* The debugger connects directly to the Cortex-M4 debug port, halts the processor, erases/writes the Flash memory, and resets the MCU automatically.\n* As long as `BOOT0` is tied to **GND via a $10\\text{ k}\\Omega$ pull-down resistor**, the MCU will run your newly flashed code immediately after the debugger releases the reset line.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Flashing via Factory Serial Bootloader (UART/SPI) - *When You DO Need the Button*\n\nIf you are **not** using an ST-LINK or SWD debugger, and instead want to flash code over a simple USB-to-UART adapter (e.g., FTDI or CP2102 connected to `USART1` or `USART2` using `STM32CubeProgrammer`):\n\n1. **Press and hold** the `BOOT0` button.\n2. **Pulse the `NRST` (Reset)** pin low to force a reset while `BOOT0` is High.\n3. Release the `BOOT0` button.\n4. The MCU enters System ROM mode, and you can flash your firmware over UART.\n5. Pulse `NRST` again without holding `BOOT0` to boot into your new program.\n\n---\n\n## 3. How Automatic USB-to-UART Auto-Reset Works (Like Arduino/ESP32)\n\nIf you've ever used boards where flashing over USB \"just works\" without pressing buttons, those boards use the USB UART adapter's **DTR** and **RTS** flow-control signals connected through a small transistor pair to automatically pull `BOOT0` HIGH and toggle `NRST` LOW right as the flashing tool starts uploading.\n\n---\n\n## Summary Recommendation\n\n* **For PCB Layout:** Keep the **$10\\text{ k}\\Omega$ pull-down resistor to GND** on `BOOT0`.\n* **Add a button or test point to 3.3V:** Keep it as a backup \"unbrick\" recovery tool in case you accidentally disable SWD pins or enter a deep stop/standby sleep mode in software where the debugger loses connection.\n* **During Daily Development:** Use SWD (`SWCLK` + `SWDIO` + `NRST` + `GND`), and you will just click \"Flash/Debug\" in STM32CubeIDE or Keil without ever touching a physical button."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 284.48 21.59 0)
